tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-2876-the-switch-bound-through-the-runtimes-header-is-told-at-the-header.hero:11:8: error[ffi_runtime_header]: `heroes_runtime.h` is the Heroes runtime's own header, the interface the C this compiler writes calls, and no program binds it: its functions count the references of the program's own values and free them, so one called from Heroes can free what the program still holds
